        "### Challenge 1: Regime Change Detection\n",
        "\n",
        "**Definition:**\n",
        "Regime change detection (or structural break detection) identifies points in time when the underlying generating process of a time series changes. In financial data like AAPL, this often corresponds to shifts between 'bull' (upward) and 'bear' (downward) markets, or periods of low vs. high volatility.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Mathematical Formula:**\n",
        "A common approach is the **Markov Switching Model**, where the observed series $y_t$ depends on an unobserved state $S_t$:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$y_t = \\mu_{S_t} + \\sigma_{S_t} \\epsilon_t$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Where:\n",
        "- $S_t \\in \\{1, 2, \\dots, K\\}$ is the regime at time $t$.\n",
        "- $\\mu_{S_t}$ and $\\sigma_{S_t}$ are the mean and standard deviation specific to that regime.\n",
        "- Transition probabilities between regimes are defined by a transition matrix $P$, where $P_{ij} = P(S_t = j | S_{t-1} = i)$."
      ]
    },
